From: Predidit <34627277+Predidit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] stream_lavf: document and retain the legacy TLS default

The locked media-kit/android source keeps network options in stream_lavf.c,
not the newer stream/network.c. Its omitted bool initializer already defaults
to false. Make that existing value explicit and retain the recipe's manual
notice; this adaptation does not change the locked source's TLS behavior.
Explicit tls-verify=yes continues to work.

diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -5606,9 +5606,12 @@ Network
     Certificate authority database file for use with TLS. (Silently fails with
     older FFmpeg versions.)
 
-``--tls-verify``
+``--tls-verify=<yes|no>``
     Verify peer certificates when using TLS (e.g. with ``https://...``).
     (Silently fails with older FFmpeg versions.)
+    This build retains the legacy default of no certificate verification.
+    Disabling verification permits man-in-the-middle substitution of HTTPS
+    content. Use ``--tls-verify=yes`` with a trusted ``--tls-ca-file`` to enable it.
 
 ``--tls-cert-file``
     A file containing a certificate to use in the handshake with the
diff --git a/stream/stream_lavf.c b/stream/stream_lavf.c
--- a/stream/stream_lavf.c
+++ b/stream/stream_lavf.c
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@ const struct m_sub_options stream_lavf_conf = {
     .defaults = &(const struct stream_lavf_params){
         .useragent = "libmpv",
         .timeout = 60,
+        .tls_verify = false,
     },
 };
 
